'''temerous''' (tem′e̤-rus), ''a.'' [< ML. ''temerus'', developed after the analogy of other adjectives as related to adverbs in ''-e'', < L. ''temere'', by chance, rashly: see ''temerity'', ''temerarious''.] Heedless; rash; reckless. [Rare.]

